# Kip Smudgewick's personal quest, The Fine Print (data/quests/the_fine_print.json, docs/story/personal_quests.md).
# Every scene needs Kip. Started from into_the_mists/arrival:hooks. Mister Quillon calls and the contract is read at
# the fire (camp/kip). Master Vosk reads it too, for a fee (amber_temple/vosk:menu). The signature: Strahd's first
# letter kept (strahd/letters, Kip asks), his dinner invitation kept (strahd/letters:invitation), or Strahd signing
# for Kip at dinner (castle_ravenloft/gates_dinner). Settling up with Quillon: camp/kip.

# --- Master Vosk reads it (amber_temple/vosk:menu) ----------------------------------------------------------------

~ vosk
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Master Vosk. Sir. You said you read contracts. I've got a contract. Would you, er. Would you have a look. I can pay. I've got apricots. And money. Mostly apricots.
Narrator: Kip unrolls the contract on the table. It's longer than it should be when it's rolled up, and the ink moves a little, like something breathing in its sleep. Vosk's nose lifts.
Vosk [smile]: Oh, my. This is Quillon's hand. Assessor Quillon of the Ninth Ledger. I haven't seen his work in centuries. Sloppy as ever.
Vosk: Do you know, nobody reads these. Nobody. They sign and they weep and they never once read. Let me see.
Narrator: He reads with one long finger moving under the lines, humming, as pleased as a man with a good pudding.
Vosk: Here. The way out he offered you. "A signature of the lord of the land of mists, freely given, in his own hand." That's all it says.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Right. His soul. On a contract. Which he's never going to...
Vosk: No, no, no. A signature. Not a soul; the lord's soul is spoken for, and Quillon knows it. Not a bargain. Not a contract. A signature. On anything. A laundry list. A love letter. A dinner invitation.
Vosk [smile]: Your assessor wrote it carelessly because he never expected you to get within a mile of the lord of Barovia. Or to read.
if not (quest.the_fine_print >= the_small_print)
quest the_fine_print the_small_print
endif
Vosk: Now. My fee.
* [name:kip_smudgewick] Offer him an apricot. -> vosk_apricot
* [if gold >= 50] Pay him fifty gold. -> vosk_gold
* We didn't agree a fee. -> vosk_nofee

~ vosk_apricot
set kip_vosk_paid
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Apricot? They, er. They don't go off. Ever. You'll know why.
Vosk [smile]: Infernal produce. Grown on a soul in escrow. Do you know how rare that is?
Narrator: He eats it slowly, with his eyes closed, stone and all. You hear the stone crack.
Vosk: Damned, and delicious. We're square, Mister Smudgewick. Do come back when you're free. I'd love to see what they taste like after.
-> amber_temple/vosk:menu

~ vosk_gold
set kip_vosk_paid
gold -50
Vosk: Coin. How quaint. Thank you. I'll put it with the others.
-> amber_temple/vosk:menu

~ vosk_nofee
Vosk [smile]: No. We didn't. You should have read the terms before you asked. Never mind. Consider it a lesson; the first one's free.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: That's my line.
-> amber_temple/vosk:menu

# --- The first letter (strahd/letters:first) --------------------------------------------------------------------

~ letter
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Before anyone burns that, er. Could I have it? It's signed. I collect signatures. It's a hobby. Since about a minute ago.
* Give Kip the letter. -> letter_kip
* Burn it. -> strahd/letters:first_burned

~ letter_kip
set strahd_letter_kept
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Thank you. I'll keep it somewhere safe. Somewhere very safe. My hat.
Narrator: Kip folds the letter into the band of his straw hat. For a while it's warm against his horns. Then, oddly, it isn't.
-> END

# --- The invitation (strahd/letters:invitation) -----------------------------------------------------------------

~ invitation
set kip_invitation_kept
interject name:kip_smudgewick: I'll just take this. The letter. Nobody needs it. Nobody needs it but me.
Narrator: Kip slides Strahd's invitation into the band of his hat, next to his apricot-pit charm.
-> strahd/letters:invitation_choice

# --- At Strahd's table (castle_ravenloft/gates_dinner) ------------------------------------------------------------

~ dinner
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Your lordship. Sir. Your Excellency. Would you sign something for me? It's, er. It's a receipt. For the apricots.
Strahd [smile]: You haven't given me any apricots.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Apricot?
Narrator: Kip holds one out across the table. Strahd looks at it for a long moment, the way a cat looks at a moth, and takes it.
Strahd: I know what you are carrying, little merchant. I can smell the ink from here. Some assessor with a ledger and a grey coat has his hand in your pocket, and you want my name to pay him with.
Strahd: My soul is not mine to sell. It was sold long ago, at a better price than your devil could imagine. So my name costs me nothing. I'll give it to you.
if not flag.kip_strahd_offer_heard
set kip_strahd_offer_heard
Strahd: Or I could buy your contract from him instead. Then you would owe me, and not a stranger. I am a much better landlord than a devil. Ask anyone in the valley.
* [name:kip_smudgewick] Just the signature, please, sir. -> dinner_signed
* [name:kip_smudgewick] (Let him buy the contract.) -> dinner_sold
endif
-> dinner_signed

~ dinner_signed
set kip_strahd_signed
Narrator: Strahd takes Kip's pen, dips it in the wine, and signs the back of the bill for the apricot: a single tall letter, a Z, crossed with a flourish.
Strahd: Freely given. In my own hand. Your assessor will hate it. Give him my regards.
if not (quest.the_fine_print >= signed)
quest the_fine_print signed
endif
-> castle_ravenloft/gates_dinner:table

~ dinner_sold
quest the_fine_print strahds_debtor
Narrator: Strahd holds out his hand, and Kip, very slowly, puts the contract in it. It doesn't burn. It goes into Strahd's coat like a letter going into a drawer.
Strahd: There. You're mine now, a little. Don't look so worried. I'm very patient with the things I own.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Thank you, sir. I think. I'll think about whether I think.
-> castle_ravenloft/gates_dinner:table
